00:15:29,915 --> 00:15:31,517
Jay: THIS IS, LIKE,
LOOKING CLOSE,

449
00:15:31,517 --> 00:15:32,751
BUT THAT'S A GOOD TRY.

450
00:15:32,751 --> 00:15:33,786
ELYSE, IT'S LOOKING GOOD.

451
00:15:33,786 --> 00:15:35,087
ALL RIGHT, NICOLE.

452
00:15:35,087 --> 00:15:36,822
Nicole: YOU'RE GONNA LAUGH
AT MY EYELASHES.

453
00:15:36,822 --> 00:15:38,290
- Jay: YEAH, YOU NEED PRACTICE.
- Nicole: YEAH.

454
00:15:38,290 --> 00:15:39,825
Jay: GISELLE?

455
00:15:39,825 --> 00:15:42,161
IT'S GREAT, BUT REMEMBER,
YESTERDAY WE TALKED ABOUT

456
00:15:42,161 --> 00:15:43,329
MINIMIZING THE WIDTH
OF YOUR FACE.

457
00:15:43,329 --> 00:15:45,064
REMEMBER HOW WE BRONZED
AND SHAPED YOUR FACE?

458
00:15:45,064 --> 00:15:46,865
Giselle: AH!
THAT'S WHAT I DID.

459
00:15:46,865 --> 00:15:49,001
Jay: ROBIN,
THIS IS PRETTY CLOSE.

460
00:15:49,001 --> 00:15:50,903
GIVEN YOUR MOOD YESTERDAY,

461
00:15:50,903 --> 00:15:52,972
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU ACTUALLY
TOOK ANYTHING IN.

462
00:15:52,972 --> 00:15:54,406
SHANNON, REMEMBER WHEN
WE WERE TALKING ABOUT

463
00:15:54,406 --> 00:15:56,141
CUTTING THE LASHES
USING A PIECE ON THE END?

464
00:15:56,141 --> 00:15:57,276
Shannon: I DID.

465
00:15:57,276 --> 00:15:59,311
Jay: YEAH, BUT YOU GOT 'EM
BACK TO FRONT.

466
00:15:59,311 --> 00:16:01,380
KESSE, THE ONLY THING
THAT I REALLY WOULD'VE DONE

467
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:02,781
IS TRY TO RIM YOUR EYES

468
00:16:02,781 --> 00:16:04,416
AND TRY TO SMOKE IT OUT
A LITTLE BIT MORE.

469
00:16:04,416 --> 00:16:08,821
SO... I HAVE TO PICK
JUST ONE WINNER WHO GETS TO GO

470
00:16:08,821 --> 00:16:12,157
TO THE INDIAN CONSULATE TONIGHT
TO MEET SOME

471
00:16:12,157 --> 00:16:16,295
VERY INFLUENTIAL PEOPLE
IN THE FASHION INDUSTRY.

472
00:16:16,295 --> 00:16:19,932
I HONESTLY HAVE TO SAY,

473
00:16:19,932 --> 00:16:21,233
ELYSE, I THINK YOU WON.

474
00:16:21,233 --> 00:16:22,268
Elyse: THANK YOU.

475
00:16:22,268 --> 00:16:23,736
Jay: YOU DID THE CLOSEST.

476
00:16:23,736 --> 00:16:25,971
SHE GOT THE EXACT NUMBER
OF LASHES I TOLD HER TO PUT ON.

477
00:16:25,971 --> 00:16:28,073
SHE PUT IT IN
THE EXACT SAME SPOT,

478
00:16:28,073 --> 00:16:30,309
SO SHE DID EXACTLY WHAT I ASKED.

479
00:16:30,309 --> 00:16:35,447
ELYSE, YOU GET TO CHOOSE
THREE GIRLS TO GO WITH YOU.

480
00:16:35,447 --> 00:16:37,016
Elyse: OKAY, NICOLE,

481
00:16:37,016 --> 00:16:39,218
THANK YOU FOR THE SCISSORS.
I CHOOSE YOU.

482
00:16:39,218 --> 00:16:40,919
ADRIANNE, THANK YOU
VERY MUCH FOR THE MASCARA.

483
00:16:40,919 --> 00:16:41,954
I CHOOSE YOU.

484
00:16:41,954 --> 00:16:43,722
THE LAST GIRL I CHOSE RANDOMLY.

485
00:16:43,722 --> 00:16:45,724
UM, SO I GUESS
IT COULD HAVE BEEN ANYONE.

486
00:16:45,724 --> 00:16:48,460
DOES ANYONE'S MOTHER'S
MAIDEN NAME START WITH A "G"?

487
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:51,830
BUT, UM, IT WAS ROBIN.

488
00:16:51,830 --> 00:16:53,332
ROBIN, I CHOOSE YOU.

489
00:16:53,332 --> 00:16:55,000
Nicole: I'M NOT
FEELING VERY GOOD.

490
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,201
- Jay: WHAT'S GOING ON HERE?
- Elyse: SHE DOESN'T WANNA GO.

491
00:16:56,201 --> 00:16:59,071
Nicole: I FIGURE IF I GO
AND I FEEL SICK WHILE I'M THERE,

492
00:16:59,071 --> 00:17:00,339
SO I'M NOT GONNA GO AND NOT
FEEL GOOD THE WHOLE TIME.

493
00:17:00,339 --> 00:17:01,540
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

494
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:03,142
Jay: SO JUST BECAUSE
YOU'RE NOT FEELING WELL,

495
00:17:03,142 --> 00:17:04,476
YOU DON'T WANNA GO?

496
00:17:04,476 --> 00:17:05,911
Nicole: SHOULD THERE BE
A BETTER REASON?

497
00:17:05,911 --> 00:17:07,880
Jay: WELL, I MEAN,
YOU DON'T LOOK DEATHLY ILL.

498
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:09,181
Nicole: NO, I'M DEFINITELY
NOT DEATHLY ILL.

499
00:17:09,181 --> 00:17:10,816
I JUST DON'T FEEL VERY GOOD.

500
00:17:10,816 --> 00:17:12,050
Jay: YOU REALIZE
WHAT YOU'RE TURNING DOWN.

501
00:17:12,050 --> 00:17:13,117
YOU'RE TURNING DOWN
AN OPPORTUNITY

502
00:17:13,117 --> 00:17:14,787
TO ADVANCE YOUR CAREER.

503
00:17:14,787 --> 00:17:16,055
I MEAN, YOU STILL GOTTA THINK
ABOUT IT.

504
00:17:16,055 --> 00:17:17,790
I MEAN, THERE ARE THOUSANDS
OF GIRLS WHO STILL

505
00:17:17,790 --> 00:17:19,358
WANNA BE IN YOUR SPOT,

506
00:17:19,358 --> 00:17:21,327
WHETHER THEY HAD
THE FLU, FEVER, WHATEVER.

507
00:17:21,327 --> 00:17:23,061
Kesse: IF IT HAD BEEN ME,
I WOULD HAVE GONE,

508
00:17:23,061 --> 00:17:24,396
NO DOUBT, NO SECOND THOUGHTS.

509
00:17:24,396 --> 00:17:26,765
Elyse: IT'S NOT WORTH
ALIENATING THE JUDGES,

510
00:17:26,765 --> 00:17:27,465
AND I DON'T THINK SHE CAME UP

511
00:17:27,465 --> 00:17:28,934
WITH A GOOD ENOUGH EXCUSE.

512
00:17:28,934 --> 00:17:29,968
Jay: THAT'S FINE
IF THAT'S YOUR DECISION,

513
00:17:29,968 --> 00:17:31,203
BUT YOU REALIZE

514
00:17:31,203 --> 00:17:32,971
YOU COULD BE PUTTING
SOMEONE ELSE AHEAD OF YOU.

515
00:17:32,971 --> 00:17:34,406
YOU COULD JUST BE CUT THIS WEEK.

516
00:17:34,406 --> 00:17:35,808
Nicole: WELL, IF I'M CUT
THIS WEEK BECAUSE OF THIS,

517
00:17:35,808 --> 00:17:37,176
THEN THAT'S SILLY.

518
00:17:37,176 --> 00:17:38,944
Jay: SO THEN IT'S SILLY
AND YOU GO BACK HOME

519
00:17:38,944 --> 00:17:42,014
AND YOU DO WHAT,
WORK AT BURGER KING?

520
00:17:42,014 --> 00:17:43,816
Nicole: YOU KNOW WHAT? OKAY.

521
00:17:43,816 --> 00:17:48,220
NO, I'M NOT GOING.

522
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:50,022
Adrianne: YOU DON'T THINK
I HAVE FAKE EYELASHES ON, RIGHT?

523
00:17:50,022 --> 00:17:51,156
Nicole: CAN YOU NOT TALK
TO ME ABOUT YOUR EYELASHES?

524
00:17:51,156 --> 00:17:52,224
I REALLY DON'T CARE.

525
00:17:52,224 --> 00:17:53,492
Adrianne: WHOA, DUDE,
I'M SORRY.

526
00:17:53,492 --> 00:17:55,494
NICOLE NOT WANTING TO GO--

527
00:17:55,494 --> 00:17:57,396
I THINK THAT WAS KINDA DUMB.

528
00:17:57,396 --> 00:17:59,064
AND IN A WAY, I THINK SHE KINDA
WANTED TO GO HOME

529
00:17:59,064 --> 00:18:00,299
AND JUST CALL HER BOYFRIEND.

530
00:18:00,299 --> 00:18:02,101
Nicole: OH, WHATEVER.

531
00:18:02,101 --> 00:18:03,836
♪♪♪

532
00:18:10,209 --> 00:18:12,978
Derek: LADIES AND GENTLEMAN,

533
00:18:12,978 --> 00:18:17,516
WELCOME TO
THE INDIAN COMMISSION.

534
00:18:17,516 --> 00:18:18,951
Robin: IT WAS JUST
AN EXPERIENCE.

535
00:18:18,951 --> 00:18:21,086
Derek: WE HAVE ALL
MY DEAR FRIENDS IN FASHION HERE.

536
00:18:21,086 --> 00:18:22,254
YOU HAVE SOME OF
THE BEST PROFESSIONALS

537
00:18:22,254 --> 00:18:23,255
IN OUR BUSINESS--

538
00:18:23,255 --> 00:18:25,257
MAXIMILLIAN TUCCI,

539
00:18:25,257 --> 00:18:26,859
JANICE COMBS,

540
00:18:26,859 --> 00:18:30,028
CONSTANCE WHITE,
A TOP FASHION JOURNALIST.

541
00:18:30,028 --> 00:18:31,430
Constance: HI, LADIES.

542
00:18:31,430 --> 00:18:33,365
Robin: WELL, I COULD TELL,
LIKE, THEY WERE VERY WEALTHY,

543
00:18:33,365 --> 00:18:36,268
AND THEY KNEW A LOT
ABOUT FASHION.

544
00:18:36,268 --> 00:18:39,071
Derek: THIS IS OUR DESIGNER
FOR THE EVENING, ANAND JON.

545
00:18:39,071 --> 00:18:41,173
ANAND'S ABSOLUTELY BRILLIANT.

546
00:18:41,173 --> 00:18:43,175
WHAT WE'RE GOING TO DO IS GET
SOME OF HIS GARMENTS ON YOU,

547
00:18:43,175 --> 00:18:44,743
AND WE'RE GOING TO CRITIQUE IT.

548
00:18:44,743 --> 00:18:48,414
♪♪♪

549
00:18:48,414 --> 00:18:49,948
Adrianne: YOU KNOW,
IF YOU'RE A MODEL,

550
00:18:49,948 --> 00:18:51,283
YOU GOTTA BE COMFORTABLE
WITH YOUR BODY,

551
00:18:51,283 --> 00:18:54,753
AND HERE I AM,
JUST BOOBS THE ENTIRE TIME,

552
00:18:54,753 --> 00:18:56,455
AND I DIDN'T CARE,
SO I HOPE THAT, LIKE,

553
00:18:56,455 --> 00:18:58,290
IT COUNTS FOR SOMETHING.

554
00:18:58,290 --> 00:18:59,358
Constance: UM, ADRIANNE--

555
00:18:59,358 --> 00:19:01,093
I REALLY LIKED HER LOOK.

556
00:19:01,093 --> 00:19:04,129
I THOUGHT SHE HAD
A SENSUOUSNESS AND SEXUALITY.

557
00:19:04,129 --> 00:19:05,197
Derek: SHE'S JUST RAIL-THIN.

558
00:19:05,197 --> 00:19:06,498
I LOVE IT.

559
00:19:06,498 --> 00:19:08,967
Constance: ELYSE, I THOUGHT,
HAD A REALLY GOOD LOOK

560
00:19:08,967 --> 00:19:10,068
FOR THE RUNWAY.

561
00:19:10,068 --> 00:19:12,438
Derek: WE HAVE
OUR GLAMOURPUSS HERE.

562
00:19:12,438 --> 00:19:14,006
Constance: ROBIN IS AN
INTERESTING CASE.

563
00:19:14,006 --> 00:19:17,776
THE INDUSTRY
FOR LARGE SIZES IS BOOMING.

564
00:19:17,776 --> 00:19:19,344
(horn honks)

565
00:19:19,344 --> 00:19:21,747
Nicole: IF NONE OF THIS
HAPPENS FOR ME,

566
00:19:21,747 --> 00:19:23,515
I THINK I'M GONNA
START CONSIDERING,

567
00:19:23,515 --> 00:19:26,418
YOU KNOW, GETTING MARRIED
AND HAVING BABIES.

568
00:19:26,418 --> 00:19:28,487
- BABY?
- Cory: Hi, honey.

569
00:19:28,487 --> 00:19:29,955
Nicole: I DON'T WANNA FIGHT,
I DON'T WANNA ARGUE WITH YOU,

570
00:19:29,955 --> 00:19:32,057
BUT I JUST--I JUST--I'M SORRY.

571
00:19:32,057 --> 00:19:33,158
I'M NOT HAPPY WITH YOU
RIGHT NOW, BABE.

572
00:19:33,158 --> 00:19:34,960
ARE YOU JUST PARTYING,
OR WHAT'S THE DEAL?

573
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:36,028
Cory: You're the one that
needs to get ahold of me

574
00:19:36,028 --> 00:19:37,062
when you have a second

575
00:19:37,062 --> 00:19:38,330
and let me know
when I can call you.

576
00:19:38,330 --> 00:19:40,332
Nicole: BABY, I HAVE
CALLED YOU EVERY SINGLE DAY,

577
00:19:40,332 --> 00:19:42,734
FOUR TIMES A DAY
FOR THE LAST SIX DAYS.

578
00:19:42,734 --> 00:19:44,736
DID YOU TRY TO CALL ME
YESTERDAY?

579
00:19:44,736 --> 00:19:45,404
- Cory: No.
- Nicole: DAY BEFORE?

580
00:19:45,404 --> 00:19:46,405
Cory: No.

581
00:19:46,405 --> 00:19:48,040
Nicole: DAY BEFORE?

582
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:49,174
Cory: No. I haven't tried
to call you at all.

583
00:19:49,174 --> 00:19:50,809
Nicole: CORY, YOU KNOW WHAT?
YOU'RE NOT BEING

584
00:19:50,809 --> 00:19:52,411
A SUPPORTIVE BOYFRIEND, CORY.

585
00:19:52,411 --> 00:19:53,278
YOU'RE REALLY NOT RIGHT NOW.

586
00:19:53,278 --> 00:19:55,280
YOU'RE NOT.

587
00:19:55,280 --> 00:19:57,416
Man: NOW YOU--
YOU'RE ALWAYS SMILING,

588
00:19:57,416 --> 00:20:00,219
BUT WHAT THAT'S TRANSLATING
TO IS DEFINITELY, LIKE,

589
00:20:00,219 --> 00:20:01,854
A SPOKESPERSON KIND OF A MODEL.

590
00:20:01,854 --> 00:20:04,089
YOU--DEFINITE RUNWAY.

591
00:20:04,089 --> 00:20:06,158
Elyse: THERE WERE A LOT
OF IMPORTANT PEOPLE THERE.

592
00:20:06,158 --> 00:20:09,928
Adrianne: I'VE BEEN REJECTED
FOR EIGHT YEARS IN THE BUSINESS,

593
00:20:09,928 --> 00:20:11,430
AND I'M JUST BEING TOLD
AT THE CONSULATE

594
00:20:11,430 --> 00:20:16,335
THAT I WAS
DEFINITE PRINT MATERIAL.

595
00:20:16,335 --> 00:20:17,970
Robin: YOU KNOW, I THINK THAT
EVERYBODY NEEDS THAT EXPOSURE,

596
00:20:17,970 --> 00:20:19,037
THAT EXPERIENCE.

597
00:20:19,037 --> 00:20:20,939
SO I THINK NICOLE DID MISS OUT.

598
00:20:20,939 --> 00:20:23,442
Jay: WITH NICOLE NOT BEING HERE,
DO ANY OF THESE WOMEN

599
00:20:23,442 --> 00:20:25,878
KNOW WHAT SHE LOOKS LIKE?

600
00:20:25,878 --> 00:20:27,446
Nicole: SO, BABE,
SO ARE YOU HAVING A GOOD TIME?

601
00:20:27,446 --> 00:20:28,847
ARE WE GROWING APART?

602
00:20:28,847 --> 00:20:30,115
TELL ME WHAT'S ON YOUR MIND.

603
00:20:30,115 --> 00:20:32,017
Cory: The only reason
I'm being a... is because

604
00:20:32,017 --> 00:20:33,519
I'm feeling really insecure
about my girlfriend

605
00:20:33,519 --> 00:20:34,486
with really hot guys
in New York.

606
00:20:34,486 --> 00:20:35,988
Nicole: OKAY.

607
00:20:35,988 --> 00:20:37,422
Cory: If I act like a...
you'll want me more.

608
00:20:37,422 --> 00:20:39,024
Nicole: NO, IF YOU ACT LIKE
A... I'M GONNA HANG UP ON YOU

609
00:20:39,024 --> 00:20:40,792
AND SAY... OFF.

610
00:20:40,792 --> 00:20:41,827
THAT'S WHAT I'M GONNA DO, CORY.

611
00:20:41,827 --> 00:20:44,830
YOUR REVERSE PSYCHOLOGY'S
...ASS.

612
00:20:44,830 --> 00:20:45,497
YOU'RE NOT
GONNA BE NICE TO ME.

613
00:20:45,497 --> 00:20:47,499
YOU'RE NOT GONNA LISTEN TO ME.

614
00:20:47,499 --> 00:20:49,268
Nicole: I HAVE TO CRY TO YOU.
I HAVE THINGS I WANNA SAY
TO YOU.

615
00:20:49,268 --> 00:20:50,836
I'M SAD. I'M LONELY.

616
00:20:50,836 --> 00:20:53,405
I MISS YOU. I NEED SUPPORT.

617
00:20:53,405 --> 00:20:54,506
SO WHAT DO YOU WANT ME TO DO?

618
00:20:54,506 --> 00:20:56,441
YOU WANT ME TO DROP OUT
RIGHT NOW?

619
00:20:56,441 --> 00:20:58,777
Cory: I don't know.

620
00:21:03,544 --> 00:21:06,948
♪♪♪

621
00:21:06,948 --> 00:21:10,084
Jon: HEY, SURPRISE.

622
00:21:10,084 --> 00:21:12,854
GOOD MORNING, WANNABE MODELS.

623
00:21:12,854 --> 00:21:14,689
WAKE UP.

624
00:21:14,689 --> 00:21:16,991
YOU GOT 15 MINUTES
TO MEET ME UPSTAIRS.

625
00:21:16,991 --> 00:21:18,267
WE'RE WORKING OUT
IN THIS BUILDING TODAY.

626
00:21:18,267 --> 00:21:20,102
Elyse: JON THE TRAINER

627
00:21:20,102 --> 00:21:22,838
IS SUPPOSED TO WHIP US ALL
INTO SHAPE AND GET US ALL

628
00:21:22,838 --> 00:21:25,274
TO TONE UP LIKE THE JUDGES
TOLD EVERYBODY TO DO.

629
00:21:25,274 --> 00:21:26,609
Jon: DRIVE IT UP. GOOD.

630
00:21:26,609 --> 00:21:29,678
Adrianne: THIS TRAINER
SO HAS ME PSYCHED,

631
00:21:29,678 --> 00:21:31,947
'CAUSE I LOVE TO WORK OUT.

632
00:21:31,947 --> 00:21:33,816
(grunts)

633
00:21:33,816 --> 00:21:36,318
Jon: ADRIANNE IS
AN EXTREME INDIVIDUAL.

634
00:21:36,318 --> 00:21:37,753
SHE IS IN PHENOMENAL CONDITION.

635
00:21:37,753 --> 00:21:40,022
ONE MORE. REAL SLOW, REAL SLOW.

636
00:21:40,022 --> 00:21:42,958
Adrianne: ROB WAS VERY,
VERY, VERY LATE,

637
00:21:42,958 --> 00:21:46,328
BECAUSE SHE WAS
PRIMPING HERSELF IN THE MIRROR.

638
00:21:46,328 --> 00:21:48,364
Jon: DID YOU JUST COME IN?

639
00:21:48,364 --> 00:21:50,332
COME HERE FOR A SECOND.

640
00:21:50,332 --> 00:21:52,668
HAVE A SEAT AGAINST THIS WALL
FOR A SECOND.

641
00:21:52,668 --> 00:21:55,204
GET INTO THIS POSITION
LIKE THIS AND JUST STAY HERE.

642
00:21:55,204 --> 00:21:57,807
THERE'S NO REASON TO BE LATE.

643
00:21:57,807 --> 00:22:02,711
DOWN LOWER. RIGHT THERE.
STAY THERE.

644
00:22:02,711 --> 00:22:04,280
Adrianne: (grunts)

645
00:22:04,280 --> 00:22:06,082
Jon: LOOK AT THAT.
SHE'S NUTS.

646
00:22:06,082 --> 00:22:07,216
THAT'S WHAT YOU GOTTA DO.

647
00:22:07,216 --> 00:22:10,152
YOU GOTTA GET SO PSYCHO
THAT YOU DO THAT.

648
00:22:10,152 --> 00:22:13,022
Adrianne: I THINK I'VE SHOWN
THAT I HAVE A LOT OF DRIVE,

649
00:22:13,022 --> 00:22:16,358
AND I HOPE MISS TYRA
AND THE REST SEE THAT.

650
00:22:16,358 --> 00:22:18,127
Jon: YOUR LEGS ARE WARM NOW?

651
00:22:18,127 --> 00:22:19,228
YOU FEEL THAT?
OKAY, COME OVER HERE.

652
00:22:19,228 --> 00:22:20,329
HAVE A SEAT RIGHT HERE.

653
00:22:20,329 --> 00:22:22,031
DO THAT NOW, OKAY?

654
00:22:22,031 --> 00:22:25,634
PUSH AS HARD AS YOU CAN
TILL YOU CAN'T DO ANY MORE.

655
00:22:25,634 --> 00:22:27,703
Robin: TO BE HONEST,
I THINK JON IS GOOD,

656
00:22:27,703 --> 00:22:29,371
BUT I DON'T KNOW.

657
00:22:29,371 --> 00:22:33,375
JUST SOME OF THE STUFF
DIDN'T REALLY FLY RIGHT WITH ME.

658
00:22:33,375 --> 00:22:35,010
Jon: ROBIN WAS SLACKING,

659
00:22:35,010 --> 00:22:36,879
AND SHE WAS LACKING
IN HER ABILITY TO DO

660
00:22:36,879 --> 00:22:38,814
THE EXERCISES EFFECTIVELY.

661
00:22:38,814 --> 00:22:41,150
SHE WAS CHEATING ON
SOME OF THEM.

662
00:22:41,150 --> 00:22:42,284
Giselle: IT JUST SEEMS LIKE
EVERYTHING THAT SHE DOES

663
00:22:42,284 --> 00:22:43,986
SHE ALWAYS HAS
SOME KIND OF ATTITUDE.

664
00:22:43,986 --> 00:22:46,889
Jon: DID YOU JUST FINISH
YOUR SET?

665
00:22:46,889 --> 00:22:48,891
DID YOU PUSH THAT SET?

666
00:22:48,891 --> 00:22:51,127
WOULD YOU BE HAPPY
WITH THE SET THAT YOU JUST DID

667
00:22:51,127 --> 00:22:52,862
IF THAT WAS THE ONLY SET
YOU COULD DO?

668
00:22:52,862 --> 00:22:54,063
IF THAT WAS
THE ONLY SET YOU COULD DO,

669
00:22:54,063 --> 00:22:55,164
YOU WOULD BE HAPPY WITH IT?

670
00:22:55,164 --> 00:22:56,699
YOU PUSHED YOURSELF HARD ENOUGH?

671
00:22:56,699 --> 00:22:59,735
COME OVER HERE.

672
00:22:59,735 --> 00:23:01,804
I'M GETTING THE FEELING
YOU'RE NOT WORKING HARD ENOUGH

673
00:23:01,804 --> 00:23:03,038
FOR SOME REASON.

674
00:23:03,038 --> 00:23:04,907
I DON'T KNOW WHY,
I'M JUST GETTING THE FEELING

675
00:23:04,907 --> 00:23:05,841
THAT YOU'RE NOT
WORKING HARD ENOUGH.

676
00:23:05,841 --> 00:23:06,942
Kesse: I THINK SHE JUST FELT

677
00:23:06,942 --> 00:23:09,345
LIKE EVERYBODY WAS JUST
PICKING ON HER.

678
00:23:09,345 --> 00:23:11,247
Adrianne: SHE GETS WHAT
SHE WANTS A LOT,

679
00:23:11,247 --> 00:23:12,948
AND WHEN SHE DOESN'T GET
WHAT SHE WANTS,

680
00:23:12,948 --> 00:23:14,850
I THINK SHE GETS UPSET.

681
00:23:14,850 --> 00:23:17,887
IF I WAS A DESIGNER
OR A PHOTOGRAPHER,

682
00:23:17,887 --> 00:23:19,989
HELL IF I'D WANNA WORK WITH HER.

683
00:23:22,024 --> 00:23:24,326
♪♪♪

684
00:23:24,326 --> 00:23:26,061
Tyra: ALL WEEK, THE GIRLS
HAVE BEEN LEARNING ABOUT
MAKEUP--

685
00:23:26,061 --> 00:23:27,830
ALL FACETS OF MAKEUP.

686
00:23:27,830 --> 00:23:29,298
SO I WANTED TO TAKE IT
TO THE NEXT LEVEL

687
00:23:29,298 --> 00:23:30,833
WITH A BEAUTY SHOOT TO SEE

688
00:23:30,833 --> 00:23:32,301
WHO HAS WHAT IT TAKES
IN FRONT OF THE CAMERA.

689
00:23:32,301 --> 00:23:34,637
AS YOU GUYS KNOW,
TODAY WE'RE DOING BEAUTY SHOTS.

690
00:23:34,637 --> 00:23:36,038
WITH BEAUTY, IT'S HERE.

691
00:23:36,038 --> 00:23:37,907
THERE'S VERY LITTLE FORGIVENESS.

692
00:23:37,907 --> 00:23:40,109
NOT EVERY MODEL CAN DO
BEAUTY SHOTS.

693
00:23:40,109 --> 00:23:42,878
SO THIS IS A VERY IMPORTANT DAY

694
00:23:42,878 --> 00:23:44,613
TO SEE WHO'S GONNA GO
TO THE NEXT LEVEL.

695
00:23:44,613 --> 00:23:46,749
AND WE'RE NOT
JUST DOING TYPICAL BEAUTY SHOTS.

696
00:23:46,749 --> 00:23:47,750
WE'RE DOING EXTREME
BEAUTY SHOTS.

697
00:23:47,750 --> 00:23:49,285
Jay: EACH AND EVERY ONE
OF YOU

698
00:23:49,285 --> 00:23:51,020
ARE GONNA HAVE A STRONG CONCEPT.

699
00:23:51,020 --> 00:23:54,323
IT'S NOT GOING TO BE
KIND OF SOFT AND PRETTY.

700
00:23:54,323 --> 00:23:56,025
SOME OF IT'S GONNA BE VERY EDGY.

701
00:23:56,025 --> 00:23:59,595
SO IT'S GONNA BE ALL ABOUT
GETTING YOUR LOOK ON

702
00:23:59,595 --> 00:24:01,664
AND THEN AS SOON AS YOU SEE IT,

703
00:24:01,664 --> 00:24:03,199
TRY TO BE THAT PERSON,

704
00:24:03,199 --> 00:24:04,300
BE THAT CHARACTER.

705
00:24:04,300 --> 00:24:07,670
Tyra: SO WE HAVE
AN AMAZING PHOTOGRAPHER HERE--

706
00:24:07,670 --> 00:24:08,971
MR. TROY WARD.

707
00:24:08,971 --> 00:24:10,839
Troy: THIS IS REALLY
JUST GONNA BE

708
00:24:10,839 --> 00:24:12,374
ABOUT WHAT YOU'RE
THINKING AND FEELING.

709
00:24:12,374 --> 00:24:13,809
IT'S GONNA BE RIGHT IN ON YOU,

710
00:24:13,809 --> 00:24:15,644
SO IT REALLY COMES
FROM THE EYES.

711
00:24:15,644 --> 00:24:18,714
AND WE HAVE ANOTHER MODEL

712
00:24:18,714 --> 00:24:20,216
THAT YOU'RE GONNA WORK WITH
THAT YOU DON'T KNOW ABOUT.

713
00:24:20,216 --> 00:24:21,350
Nicole: I'M LIKE,
KIND OF, LIKE, WONDERING,

714
00:24:21,350 --> 00:24:22,384
MAYBE IT'S SOMEONE FAMOUS.

715
00:24:22,384 --> 00:24:24,820
Troy: WE'VE BROUGHT MODELS IN

716
00:24:24,820 --> 00:24:27,923
FROM ALL OVER THE WORLD
TO BE WITH US HERE.

717
00:24:27,923 --> 00:24:30,059
Nicole: AND THEY WALK IN
WITH THESE HUGE SNAKES.

718
00:24:30,059 --> 00:24:32,695
OH, MY GOD. I ALMOST CRIED.

719
00:24:32,695 --> 00:24:34,330
Adrianne: I MISS MY SNAKE
SO MUCH.

720
00:24:34,330 --> 00:24:35,898
I HAVE A SNAKE NAMED BRIGITTA,

721
00:24:35,898 --> 00:24:37,099
AND IT'S A BALL PYTHON.

722
00:24:37,099 --> 00:24:38,834
Troy: REALLY?
SO YOU'LL BE RIGHT AT HOME.

723
00:24:38,834 --> 00:24:39,868
Adrianne: THE OTHER GIRLS--

724
00:24:39,868 --> 00:24:40,936
THEY WERE ALL LIKE,

725
00:24:40,936 --> 00:24:43,839
"OOH-WEE.
THEY BROUGHT IN A SNAKE.

726
00:24:43,839 --> 00:24:45,074
I AIN'T TAKING PICTURES
WITH A SNAKE."

727
00:24:45,074 --> 00:24:47,009
Robin: I'VE NEVER TOUCHED
A SNAKE BEFORE.

728
00:24:47,009 --> 00:24:48,644
I DON'T PLAY WITH REPTILES,

729
00:24:48,644 --> 00:24:50,846
AND, YOU KNOW, AMPHIBIANS
AND ALL THAT.

730
00:24:50,846 --> 00:24:52,047
Troy: DO YOU FEEL GORGEOUS?

731
00:24:52,047 --> 00:24:53,082
Robin: YEAH.

732
00:24:53,082 --> 00:24:54,350
Troy: YOU HAVE TO BELIEVE IT,

733
00:24:54,350 --> 00:24:55,384
'CAUSE IF YOU DON'T BELIEVE IT,
I WON'T BELIEVE IT.

734
00:24:55,384 --> 00:24:56,885
Robin: I THOUGHT
THAT WAS THAT SNAKE.

735
00:24:56,885 --> 00:24:59,955
(laughter)

736
00:24:59,955 --> 00:25:01,724
Troy: THERE'S A LOT
OF EMOTION IN YOUR EYES NOW.

737
00:25:01,724 --> 00:25:02,725
THAT'S GOOD, BABY.

738
00:25:02,725 --> 00:25:03,659
I BELIEVE IT.

739
00:25:03,659 --> 00:25:04,960
Tyra: WITH THE SNAKES INVOLVED,

740
00:25:04,960 --> 00:25:07,096
I WAS LOOKING
FOR SOMEONE THAT COULD STILL

741
00:25:07,096 --> 00:25:09,665
HAVE THE CONCENTRATION TO SELL
THAT PICTURE GORGEOUSLY

742
00:25:09,665 --> 00:25:11,867
RIGHT HERE WITHOUT GOING,
"EHH."

743
00:25:11,867 --> 00:25:14,169
YOU ARE SO MUCH BIGGER
THAN THE SNAKE.

744
00:25:14,169 --> 00:25:15,938
LET'S TRY THAT.

745
00:25:15,938 --> 00:25:17,239
Robin: I WEAR
SNAKESKIN BOOTS, BUT,

746
00:25:17,239 --> 00:25:21,377
YOU KNOW, I DON'T HAVE TO SEE IT
AND FEEL IT AND... MM.

747
00:25:21,377 --> 00:25:22,845
IT JUST WASN'T...

748
00:25:22,845 --> 00:25:25,614
ECCH! OOH, GET HIM, GET HIM,

749
00:25:25,614 --> 00:25:26,915
GET HIM, GET HIM, GET HIM.

750
00:25:26,915 --> 00:25:30,252
I HAD TO CALL ON JESUS,
I DON'T KNOW HOW MANY TIMES.

751
00:25:30,252 --> 00:25:33,389
OOH, JESUS, JESUS, JESUS.

752
00:25:33,389 --> 00:25:34,390
Woman: TAKE A BREATH.
TAKE A BREATH.

753
00:25:34,390 --> 00:25:35,791
Robin: JESUS.

754
00:25:35,791 --> 00:25:37,960
OOH, IT'S TICKLING
UP UNDER MY ARM.

755
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:39,595
Troy: ROBIN WAS A LITTLE BIT

756
00:25:39,595 --> 00:25:42,264
FROZEN BY EVERYTHING
THAT WAS GOING ON AROUND HER,

757
00:25:42,264 --> 00:25:43,899
BUT SHE'S BEAUTIFUL.

758
00:25:43,899 --> 00:25:45,200
I MEAN, SHE'S DEFINITELY
VERY BEAUTIFUL.

759
00:25:45,200 --> 00:25:47,169
Robin: THE END PRODUCT

760
00:25:47,169 --> 00:25:49,938
IS GLAMOROUS,
BUT WHAT IT TAKES TO GET TO THAT

761
00:25:49,938 --> 00:25:51,273
IS NOT SO GLAMOROUS.

762
00:25:51,273 --> 00:25:53,842
Troy: THANK YOU SO MUCH.

763
00:25:53,842 --> 00:25:55,678
IT'S ALMOST LIKE
GILDING A FRAME.

764
00:25:55,678 --> 00:25:58,247
Tyra: EVERY GIRL WAS GIVEN
A DIFFERENT CHARACTER,

765
00:25:58,247 --> 00:26:00,149
AND I WAS WATCHING THEM TO SEE

766
00:26:00,149 --> 00:26:02,951
HOW WELL YOU CAN EXPRESS
THAT CHARACTER

767
00:26:02,951 --> 00:26:04,153
THROUGH THE CAMERA LENS.

768
00:26:04,153 --> 00:26:06,121
Troy: RIGHT THERE.
OKAY, GOOD.

769
00:26:06,121 --> 00:26:07,756
ALMOST LIKE A BIRD.

770
00:26:07,756 --> 00:26:08,791
YOU'VE JUST POPPED OUT
OF AN EGG.

771
00:26:08,791 --> 00:26:11,960
THAT'S IT. NICE. BEAUTIFUL.

772
00:26:11,960 --> 00:26:14,129
THAT'S GREAT, ELYSE.
I LOVE IT. RIGHT THERE.

773
00:26:14,129 --> 00:26:19,635
ELYSE IS VERY AWARE OF HER BODY,

774
00:26:19,635 --> 00:26:21,203
AND SHE THINKS
ABOUT THE SHOT.

775
00:26:21,203 --> 00:26:23,205
TAKE A DEEP BREATH,
JUST RELAX.

776
00:26:23,205 --> 00:26:27,676
GONNA BE FINE.

777
00:26:27,676 --> 00:26:28,944
BEAUTIFUL. THAT'S IT.

778
00:26:28,944 --> 00:26:31,246
Tyra: A LITTLE BIT MORE
"I'M SO CUTE."

779
00:26:31,246 --> 00:26:32,915
SMILE WITH YOUR EYES
A LITTLE BIT.

780
00:26:32,915 --> 00:26:33,949
Troy: GOOD. RIGHT THERE.

781
00:26:33,949 --> 00:26:35,184
KESSE'S GOOD.

782
00:26:35,184 --> 00:26:37,286
SHE'S GOT THE SORT OF LIKE
DOE-LIKE LOOK ABOUT HER.

783
00:26:37,286 --> 00:26:38,987
Tyra: WE GOT IT.

784
00:26:38,987 --> 00:26:41,857
♪♪♪

785
00:26:45,828 --> 00:26:47,863
Troy: BEAUTIFUL.

786
00:26:47,863 --> 00:26:49,932
THE THING ABOUT EBONY
IS HER SKIN.

787
00:26:49,932 --> 00:26:50,933
I MEAN, YOU CAN FAKE IT

788
00:26:50,933 --> 00:26:52,234
A LITTLE BIT WITH RETOUCHING.

789
00:26:52,234 --> 00:26:54,269
BUT RETOUCHING'S EXPENSIVE.

790
00:26:54,269 --> 00:26:55,971
Adrianne: THAT IS SO COOL.

791
00:26:55,971 --> 00:26:59,041
Tyra: VERY '80s.

792
00:26:59,041 --> 00:27:01,043
Troy: SHANNON'S GOT
A REALLY BEAUTIFUL LOOK.

793
00:27:01,043 --> 00:27:03,979
I THINK SHE ACTUALLY LOOKS
BETTER ON CAMERA

794
00:27:03,979 --> 00:27:06,215
THAN SHE DID
WHEN I JUST LOOKED AT HER.

795
00:27:06,215 --> 00:27:08,016
Tyra: YOURS LOOKS GREAT.

796
00:27:08,016 --> 00:27:09,318
♪♪♪

797
00:27:09,318 --> 00:27:11,687
Tyra: YEAH, GISELLE,

798
00:27:11,687 --> 00:27:12,654
DON'T PUSH YOUR CHIN SO FORWARD

799
00:27:12,654 --> 00:27:13,689
THAT YOU LOSE YOUR NECK.

800
00:27:13,689 --> 00:27:15,224
Troy: BEAUTIFUL.

801
00:27:15,224 --> 00:27:17,659
GISELLE WAS VERY BRAVE.

802
00:27:17,659 --> 00:27:19,728
SHE'S VERY EXOTIC. BEAUTIFUL.

803
00:27:19,728 --> 00:27:20,863
BEAUTIFUL.
SHE'S VERY GOOD.

804
00:27:20,863 --> 00:27:22,364
- HOLD ON.
- Giselle: IT'S CHOKING ME.

805
00:27:22,364 --> 00:27:23,599
Troy: THAT'S RIGHT.

806
00:27:23,599 --> 00:27:26,068
Giselle: THE SNAKE'S PRETTY.

807
00:27:26,068 --> 00:27:28,270
Tyra: YOU DON'T THINK
YOU LOOK PRETTY?

808
00:27:28,270 --> 00:27:31,240
Nicole: MY WORST FEAR
IS SNAKES, RIGHT?

809
00:27:31,240 --> 00:27:32,808
NEVER, EVER THINKING THAT THEY

810
00:27:32,808 --> 00:27:34,209
WOULD EVER DO ANYTHING
LIKE THIS.

811
00:27:34,209 --> 00:27:35,878
I MEAN, THAT'S JUST,
YOU KNOW, WEIRD.

812
00:27:35,878 --> 00:27:37,212
OH, BOY.

813
00:27:37,212 --> 00:27:39,815
- Troy: HE DOESN'T EXIST.
- Nicole: OKAY.

814
00:27:39,815 --> 00:27:41,984
OH, WHERE'S THE HEAD
OF THE SNAKE?

815
00:27:41,984 --> 00:27:43,952
THE ONLY REASON THAT I WAS OKAY

816
00:27:43,952 --> 00:27:45,187
WITH HAVING A SNAKE
AROUND MY NECK IS 'CAUSE

817
00:27:45,187 --> 00:27:47,923
I DON'T WANT, YOU KNOW,
ANY OF MY DECISIONS

818
00:27:47,923 --> 00:27:49,725
WHILE I'M HERE
TO AFFECT THE OUTCOME OF WHETHER

819
00:27:49,725 --> 00:27:50,793
OR NOT I MAKE IT TO THE END.

820
00:27:50,793 --> 00:27:52,294
Troy: GOOD. THAT'S BEAUTIFUL.

821
00:27:52,294 --> 00:27:53,829
BEAUTIFUL.

822
00:27:53,829 --> 00:27:56,832
GIVE ME JUST A LITTLE HINT
OF A SMILE.

823
00:27:56,832 --> 00:27:58,333
REALLY GIVE ME THE EYES THERE.

824
00:27:58,333 --> 00:27:59,735
Tyra: YOUR EYES
ARE A LITTLE DEAD.

825
00:27:59,735 --> 00:28:01,970
SMILE WITH YOUR EYES
AND CLOSE YOUR MOUTH.

826
00:28:01,970 --> 00:28:03,772
Troy: NICOLE WAS
A LITTLE BIT LIMITED

827
00:28:03,772 --> 00:28:05,274
IN THE RANGE
THAT SHE WOULD GIVE ME.

828
00:28:05,274 --> 00:28:07,009
THINK OF SOMETHING REALLY GOOD,

829
00:28:07,009 --> 00:28:09,945
LIKE GETTING THIS SNAKE
OFF YOUR SHOULDERS.

830
00:28:09,945 --> 00:28:11,046
OKAY.

831
00:28:11,046 --> 00:28:11,880
Adrianne: I'M GONNA LOOK HOT.

832
00:28:11,880 --> 00:28:14,783
Tyra: I FEEL LIKE
I'M GIVING HER A NOSE JOB.

833
00:28:14,783 --> 00:28:16,852
Adrianne: THEY CALL IT
"THE MASK OF ZORRO."

834
00:28:16,852 --> 00:28:18,053
IT WAS, LIKE, PURPLE,

835
00:28:18,053 --> 00:28:19,054
AND IT WAS COOL.

836
00:28:19,054 --> 00:28:20,622
I LOOKED LIKE THE HAMBURGLAR.

837
00:28:23,492 --> 00:28:24,793
Troy: NICE HAVING TYRA HERE
HELPING YOU.

838
00:28:24,793 --> 00:28:25,928
IT'S LIKE HAVING MICHAEL JORDAN

839
00:28:25,928 --> 00:28:28,497
TEACH YOU HOW TO SHOOT
FREE THROWS.

840
00:28:28,497 --> 00:28:30,232
Tyra: OKAY. SNAKE!

841
00:28:30,232 --> 00:28:32,000
Adrianne: I HAVE A SNAKE,

842
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:33,802
AND I WAS THE ONLY ONE
THAT WASN'T A PUSS ABOUT IT,

843
00:28:33,802 --> 00:28:35,671
BECAUSE I LOVE SNAKES.

844
00:28:35,671 --> 00:28:37,539
AW.

845
00:28:37,539 --> 00:28:39,842
Woman: LIKE... (hissing)

846
00:28:39,842 --> 00:28:41,076
Troy: YEAH, THAT'S IT.

847
00:28:41,076 --> 00:28:42,244
THINK REALLY STRONG, ADRIANNE.

848
00:28:42,244 --> 00:28:45,080
YOU'RE LIKE SUPERWOMAN.

849
00:28:45,080 --> 00:28:47,516
I THINK IF WAS GONNA BOOK
A GIRL TODAY BASED ON

850
00:28:47,516 --> 00:28:48,517
WHERE THEY ARE RIGHT NOW,

851
00:28:48,517 --> 00:28:50,152
I WOULD PROBABLY PICK ADRIANNE.

852
00:28:50,152 --> 00:28:51,220
SHE'S VERY BEAUTIFUL.

853
00:28:51,220 --> 00:28:52,521
SHE HAS A GOOD TIME.

854
00:28:52,521 --> 00:28:55,257
I THINK IT WOULD BE FUN
TO WORK WITH HER.

855
00:28:55,257 --> 00:28:56,158
OKAY, I THINK WE GOT IT.

856
00:28:56,158 --> 00:28:57,159
YOU LOOK GORGEOUS.

857
00:28:57,159 --> 00:28:58,227
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

858
00:28:58,227 --> 00:29:01,830
I MEAN, THAT'S LIKE A COVER.

859
00:29:01,830 --> 00:29:03,065
Tyra: THAT'S A WRAP.

860
00:29:03,065 --> 00:29:07,035
♪♪♪

861
00:29:07,035 --> 00:29:08,804
Kesse: "TOMORROW SEVEN OF YOU

862
00:29:08,804 --> 00:29:11,273
"WILL CONTINUE ON TO BECOME
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

863
00:29:11,273 --> 00:29:12,975
ONE OF YOU WILL BE ELIMINATED."

864
00:29:12,975 --> 00:29:14,276
Giselle: OH, NO.

865
00:29:14,276 --> 00:29:17,779
THEY WERE STARING AT
YOUR PICTURES FOREVER, NICOLE.

866
00:29:17,779 --> 00:29:20,082
- Nicole: WHAT DOES THAT MEAN?
- Giselle: I DON'T KNOW.

867
00:29:20,082 --> 00:29:22,751
YOU'RE BEING ELIMINATED, NICOLE,
THAT'S WHAT IT MEANS.

868
00:29:22,751 --> 00:29:24,052
Nicole: YEAH, RIGHT.

869
00:29:24,052 --> 00:29:26,255
I AIN'T GOING NOWHERE.
I STILL HAVE TWO MORE WEEKS'

870
00:29:26,255 --> 00:29:27,723
WORTH OF CLOTHES, BABY.

871
00:29:27,723 --> 00:29:29,758
Giselle: YOU BETTER WORK IT OUT.

872
00:29:29,758 --> 00:29:31,860
Adrianne: I THINK
I DID A GOOD JOB THIS WEEK.

873
00:29:31,860 --> 00:29:33,962
I KNOW I'M NOT GONNA GET
ELIMINATED,

874
00:29:33,962 --> 00:29:36,765
BECAUSE I JUST TRIED
TOO DAMN HARD,

875
00:29:36,765 --> 00:29:39,968
AND I THINK THAT GOD'S
GONNA BLESS ME.

876
00:29:44,873 --> 00:29:48,610
- Ebony: ADRIANNE IS SICK, GUYS.
- Shannon: WHAT?

877
00:29:48,610 --> 00:29:49,778
Ebony: SHE'S LIKE,
"YOU HAVEN'T NOTICED?"

878
00:29:49,778 --> 00:29:51,013
SHE'S BEEN SO QUIET,
LIKE, FOR THREE HOURS.

879
00:29:51,013 --> 00:29:55,150
LISTEN. NOTHING.

880
00:29:55,150 --> 00:29:56,818
Adrianne: I JUST DON'T WANNA
THROW UP IN A BAG.

881
00:29:56,818 --> 00:29:58,120
Ebony: OH. WATCH IT.

882
00:29:58,120 --> 00:30:01,623
SHE DOESN'T FEEL GOOD.

883
00:30:01,623 --> 00:30:02,758
POOR BABY.

884
00:30:02,758 --> 00:30:04,092
Giselle: I GO OVER
AND CHECK ON HER,

885
00:30:04,092 --> 00:30:07,663
AND SHE'S IN THE BATHROOM, LIKE,
SHIVERING AND CRYING.

886
00:30:07,663 --> 00:30:09,665
IT JUST REALLY HURTS ME

887
00:30:09,665 --> 00:30:10,699
TO SEE HER SICK LIKE THAT,

888
00:30:10,699 --> 00:30:12,868
ESPECIALLY WHEN
TONIGHT'S ELIMINATION.

889
00:30:12,868 --> 00:30:15,504
Adrianne: I DON'T WANNA
STAND UP STRAIGHT, PLEASE.

890
00:30:15,504 --> 00:30:17,172
Giselle: PUT THE BLANKET ON HER.

891
00:30:17,172 --> 00:30:18,974
SHE'S BEING SHIPPED OFF
TO THE HOSPITAL RIGHT NOW,

892
00:30:18,974 --> 00:30:20,208
AND IT'S REALLY SAD.

893
00:30:20,208 --> 00:30:21,944
Adrianne: (groans)

894
00:30:21,944 --> 00:30:25,047
I'M FEELING SO BAD,
AND I DON'T WANNA WALK.

895
00:30:25,047 --> 00:30:27,282
(sobbing)

896
00:30:31,653 --> 00:30:32,955
Kesse: ADRIANNE'S SO SICK.

897
00:30:32,955 --> 00:30:34,990
I FEEL SO BAD,
I'VE NEVER SEEN HER LIKE THAT.

898
00:30:34,990 --> 00:30:36,592
Adrianne: I HATE HOSPITALS.

899
00:30:36,592 --> 00:30:40,862
I DON'T WANNA GO.

900
00:30:40,862 --> 00:30:42,164
(moaning)

901
00:30:53,224 --> 00:30:54,501
♪♪♪

902
00:30:54,501 --> 00:30:55,969
Robin: ELIMINATION DAY,

903
00:30:55,969 --> 00:30:57,037
AND EVERYBODY'S JUST
GETTING READY.

904
00:30:57,037 --> 00:30:58,605
ADRIANNE GOT SICK TODAY.

905
00:30:58,605 --> 00:31:00,373
Kesse: I TOLD HER THAT
I LOVED HER BEFORE SHE LEFT.

906
00:31:00,373 --> 00:31:02,142
YOU KNOW, THAT'S MY GIRL,

907
00:31:02,142 --> 00:31:05,011
SO, UM, I REALLY HOPE
SHE FEELS BETTER.

908
00:31:05,011 --> 00:31:06,546
Tyra: I WOULD NEVER CUT
ADRIANNE FOR BEING SICK,

909
00:31:06,546 --> 00:31:09,416
BUT UNFORTUNATELY, THE JUDGES

910
00:31:09,416 --> 00:31:12,385
CAME TO THE DECISION THAT
IF SHE WAS NOT PRESENT

911
00:31:12,385 --> 00:31:14,621
DURING THE JUDGING,
SHE WOULD BE ELIMINATED

912
00:31:14,621 --> 00:31:16,623
BECAUSE IT WOULDN'T BE FAIR
TO THE OTHER GIRLS

913
00:31:16,623 --> 00:31:18,024
THAT WOULD BE PRESENT.

914
00:31:18,024 --> 00:31:19,993
Shannon: HEY, ADRIANNE'S
GONNA MISS THIS ONE.

915
00:31:19,993 --> 00:31:21,228
THAT'S GOTTA SUCK,
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

916
00:31:21,228 --> 00:31:22,929
- 'CAUSE SHE'S SICK.
- Kesse: YEAH.

917
00:31:26,399 --> 00:31:29,269
Adrianne: THE DOCTOR TOLD ME
IT WAS A SEVERE CASE

918
00:31:29,269 --> 00:31:30,604
OF FOOD POISONING.

919
00:31:30,604 --> 00:31:33,306
I FAKED BEING BETTER
TO GET OUT OF THE HOSPITAL.

920
00:31:33,306 --> 00:31:35,609
I'M NOT GONNA MISS ELIMINATION.

921
00:31:35,609 --> 00:31:37,978
THERE'S NO WAY.

922
00:31:37,978 --> 00:31:40,480
RIGHT NOW I FEEL
SO INCREDIBLY WEAK.

923
00:31:40,480 --> 00:31:42,315
I CAN'T OPEN MY EYES.

924
00:31:42,315 --> 00:31:45,518
I FEEL LIKE I CAN'T LIFT
2 POUNDS.

925
00:31:45,518 --> 00:31:47,220
I FEEL LIKE HELL.

926
00:31:47,220 --> 00:31:49,522
Elyse: I FULLY EXPECTED

927
00:31:49,522 --> 00:31:52,926
ADRIANNE TO BE AT THE JUDGING
NO MATTER HOW SICK SHE WAS.

928
00:31:52,926 --> 00:31:54,961
I KNEW THAT SHE WOULD INSIST
ON BEING THERE.

929
00:31:54,961 --> 00:31:57,998
SHE'S A TOUGH BROAD,

930
00:31:57,998 --> 00:31:59,633
AS SHE WOULD SAY
IN HER OWN WORDS.

931
00:31:59,633 --> 00:32:01,635
Tyra: WELCOME, LADIES.

932
00:32:01,635 --> 00:32:03,703
IT'S BEEN ANOTHER EVENTFUL WEEK

933
00:32:03,703 --> 00:32:06,640
IN YOUR JOURNEY IN BECOMING
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL,

934
00:32:06,640 --> 00:32:08,642
AND I KNOW THIS WEEK
HAS BEEN HARD-CORE.

935
00:32:08,642 --> 00:32:10,143
A LOT OF YOU GUYS HAVE SAID,

936
00:32:10,143 --> 00:32:11,945
"OH, YEAH, THIS IS NICE.
THIS IS FUN,"

937
00:32:11,945 --> 00:32:14,147
BUT THIS WEEK GOT SERIOUS.

938
00:32:14,147 --> 00:32:16,249
SO NOW YOU SEE
THIS BUSINESS IS NO GAME.

939
00:32:16,249 --> 00:32:18,051
BUT NOW IT'S TIME
TO MAKE OUR THIRD CUT

940
00:32:18,051 --> 00:32:20,353
TOWARDS DETERMINING WHO WILL BE

941
00:32:20,353 --> 00:32:22,355
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

942
00:32:22,355 --> 00:32:25,158
THE WINNER WILL RECEIVE
A CONTRACT WITH REVLON,

943
00:32:25,158 --> 00:32:26,459
A FASHION SPREAD
WITH "MARIE CLAIRE"

944
00:32:26,459 --> 00:32:29,329
AND A CONTRACT WITH ONE
OF THE WORLD'S TOP AGENCIES--

945
00:32:29,329 --> 00:32:30,530
WILHELMINA.

946
00:32:30,530 --> 00:32:32,632
SO WE HAVE FIVE JUDGES.

947
00:32:32,632 --> 00:32:34,000
FIRST, WE HAVE JANICE DICKINSON,

948
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:35,035
ONE OF THE WORLD'S
FIRST SUPERMODELS,

949
00:32:35,035 --> 00:32:36,269
BEAU QUILLIAN,

950
00:32:36,269 --> 00:32:38,305
THE FASHION EDITOR
AT "MARIE CLAIRE" MAGAZINE,

951
00:32:38,305 --> 00:32:39,639
KIMORA LEE SIMMONS,

952
00:32:39,639 --> 00:32:42,242
THE OWNER AND CREATIVE DIRECTOR
OF BABY PHAT FASHIONS,

953
00:32:42,242 --> 00:32:45,145
AND THIS WEEK'S SPECIAL JUDGE--

954
00:32:45,145 --> 00:32:46,279
MR. JAY MANUEL.

955
00:32:46,279 --> 00:32:47,881
JAY HAS DEVISED A TEST.

956
00:32:47,881 --> 00:32:50,116
Jay: TAKE A LOOK
AT THE MONITOR.

957
00:32:50,116 --> 00:32:51,251
- Tyra: C'EST MOI.
- Janice: WHOA!

958
00:32:51,251 --> 00:32:53,586
- Kimora: THIS IS TYRA!
- Janice: OW!

959
00:32:53,586 --> 00:32:54,854
Jay: TYRA AND I DID
THIS LOOK.

960
00:32:54,854 --> 00:32:56,156
WE WERE HAVING FUN ON A SHOOT,

961
00:32:56,156 --> 00:32:59,125
AND WE WANTED TO DO
EXTREME BEAUTY, SO WE DID IT.

962
00:32:59,125 --> 00:33:00,160
Tyra: YOU'RE NOT
ALWAYS GONNA HAVE

963
00:33:00,160 --> 00:33:02,395
A GREAT MAKEUP ARTIST LIKE JAY,

964
00:33:02,395 --> 00:33:05,031
SO YOU NEED TO KNOW HOW TO DO
ALL DIFFERENT STYLES OF MAKEUP.

965
00:33:05,031 --> 00:33:06,866
Jay: SO THE TEST IS

966
00:33:06,866 --> 00:33:09,336
YOU'RE GOING TO HAVE 20 MINUTES.

967
00:33:09,336 --> 00:33:11,404
YOU'RE EACH GONNA RECEIVE
A COPY OF THE PHOTOGRAPH.

968
00:33:11,404 --> 00:33:14,507
WE'RE GONNA JUDGE TO SEE
WHO CAN GET THE CLOSEST

969
00:33:14,507 --> 00:33:16,576
TO THIS LOOK.

970
00:33:16,576 --> 00:33:17,610
Tyra: GO.

971
00:33:17,610 --> 00:33:19,179
♪♪♪

972
00:33:34,160 --> 00:33:35,595
Adrianne: MY TUMMY
JUST REALLY HURTS STILL,

973
00:33:35,595 --> 00:33:36,963
AND I'M REALLY WEAK.

974
00:33:36,963 --> 00:33:39,399
AND I'M REALLY PROUD OF MYSELF,

975
00:33:39,399 --> 00:33:40,200
AND I HOPE
I DON'T GET ELIMINATED.

976
00:33:41,935 --> 00:33:43,403
Janice: THERE YOU GO.

977
00:33:43,403 --> 00:33:44,904
Jay: WHOA!

978
00:33:44,904 --> 00:33:46,339
Beau: ADRIANNE, ARE YOU OKAY?

979
00:33:46,339 --> 00:33:47,640
Adrianne: I THINK
I HAD FOOD POISONING.

980
00:33:47,640 --> 00:33:50,009
THAT'S WHAT THEY SAID, SO...

981
00:33:50,009 --> 00:33:51,277
Janice: THE FACT OF
THE MATTER THAT YOU SHOWED UP

982
00:33:51,277 --> 00:33:54,614
IS WHAT IT TAKES TO BE A MODEL
AND A SUPERMODEL.

983
00:33:54,614 --> 00:33:56,349
WELL DONE. I APPLAUD THAT.

984
00:33:56,349 --> 00:33:57,417
Jay: OH, YEAH,
I CAN'T BELIEVE--

985
00:33:57,417 --> 00:33:58,418
THE FACE LOOKS AMAZING.

986
00:33:58,418 --> 00:33:59,953
Tyra: THE FACE IS GOOD.

987
00:33:59,953 --> 00:34:01,187
NOW WE'RE GONNA CHECK OUT
YOUR BEAUTY CLOSE-UP SHOOT

988
00:34:01,187 --> 00:34:02,956
THAT YOU DID
WITH YOUR EXTREME MAKEUP.

989
00:34:02,956 --> 00:34:05,058
- Adrianne: WHOA.
- Janice: MY!

990
00:34:05,058 --> 00:34:06,559
Tyra: WHAT DO YOU THINK
ABOUT YOUR PICTURE?

991
00:34:06,559 --> 00:34:07,994
Adrianne: I THINK
IT'S REALLY GOOD.

992
00:34:07,994 --> 00:34:09,195
Janice: WELL,
YOU LOOK AMAZING.

993
00:34:09,195 --> 00:34:10,463
Jay: YOU DIDN'T EVEN
LOOK SCARED OF IT.

994
00:34:10,463 --> 00:34:11,864
I JUST LOVE YOUR CONFIDENCE.

995
00:34:11,864 --> 00:34:13,900
Beau: YOU LOOK GORGEOUS,
VERY ENGAGED.

996
00:34:13,900 --> 00:34:15,869
Adrianne: THANK YOU SO MUCH,
GUYS.

997
00:34:17,603 --> 00:34:19,072
Tyra: WORK IT OUT!

998
00:34:19,072 --> 00:34:20,139
Jay: ON THE MAKEOVER DAY,

999
00:34:20,139 --> 00:34:21,908
WE STARTED PUTTING IN
EXTENSIONS.

1000
00:34:21,908 --> 00:34:23,143
Kimora: I LOVE THE HAIR.

1001
00:34:23,143 --> 00:34:24,377
Tyra: SO WHEN YOU'RE
IN THE CLUB,

1002
00:34:24,377 --> 00:34:25,978
"ALL THE GIRLS
WITH THE HAIR WEAVES,

1003
00:34:25,978 --> 00:34:27,112
RAISE THEIR HANDS!"

1004
00:34:27,112 --> 00:34:28,415
KESSE'S GONNA BE LIKE, "HEY!"

1005
00:34:28,415 --> 00:34:30,650
All: (laughing)

1006
00:34:30,650 --> 00:34:32,118
Tyra: GO TO YOUR PHOTO.

1007
00:34:32,118 --> 00:34:33,485
Janice: "THERE'S A FRICKIN'
SNAKE ON MY SHOULDER,

1008
00:34:33,485 --> 00:34:34,888
AND THIS IS WHAT'S
REGISTERED ON MY FACE."

1009
00:34:36,623 --> 00:34:39,458
Tyra: HELLO, NICOLE.

1010
00:34:39,458 --> 00:34:41,127
Beau: UM, IT LOOKS LIKE YOU
REALLY GAVE IT A GOOD TRY TO ME.

1011
00:34:41,127 --> 00:34:42,328
Nicole: THANK YOU.

1012
00:34:42,328 --> 00:34:44,164
Kimora: IT'S A BIT
TOO NATURAL AND TOO LIGHT.

1013
00:34:44,164 --> 00:34:45,532
IT SEEMED LIKE YOU WERE
SCARED OF IT.

1014
00:34:45,532 --> 00:34:47,100
Nicole: I KNOW WHAT YOU MEAN.

1015
00:34:47,100 --> 00:34:48,201
I SAW--I LOOKED AT A COUPLE
OF THE OTHER GIRLS,

1016
00:34:48,201 --> 00:34:49,969
I'M LIKE,
I COULD'VE GONE WAY MORE CRAZY.

1017
00:34:49,969 --> 00:34:51,538
Tyra: ALL RIGHT, SO NOW
WE HAVE YOUR PHOTO SHOOT SHOT.

1018
00:34:51,538 --> 00:34:53,373
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

1019
00:34:53,373 --> 00:34:55,007
Nicole: IT'S GORGEOUS,
I LOVE IT.

1020
00:34:55,007 --> 00:34:57,110
Jay: THE LOOK IN YOUR EYES--
IT'S JUST--I DON'T KNOW.

1021
00:34:57,110 --> 00:34:58,945
- Tyra: A LITTLE BLANK?
- Nicole: REALLY?

1022
00:34:58,945 --> 00:35:00,313
Tyra: IT WAS A LITTLE
DIFFICULT CHOOSING YOUR PICTURES

1023
00:35:00,313 --> 00:35:03,616
BECAUSE A LOT OF THEM DIDN'T
HAVE LIFE IN THE EYES.

1024
00:35:03,616 --> 00:35:05,552
THAT'S SOMETHING THAT YOU
REALLY HAVE TO WORK ON

1025
00:35:05,552 --> 00:35:07,487
AND REALLY TRY TO PULL
OUT OF YOURSELF,

1026
00:35:07,487 --> 00:35:09,322
BECAUSE YOUR EYES
TEND TO GO VERY DEAD.

1027
00:35:09,322 --> 00:35:11,925
♪♪♪

1028
00:35:11,925 --> 00:35:13,359
- Tyra: ELYSE.
- Elyse: HI.

1029
00:35:13,359 --> 00:35:14,894
Tyra: I THINK YOU WENT
A LITTLE TOO CONSERVATIVE.

1030
00:35:14,894 --> 00:35:16,296
Jay: AND I'M SO SURPRISED

1031
00:35:16,296 --> 00:35:18,164
'CAUSE YOU WON
THE MAKEUP CHALLENGE.

1032
00:35:18,164 --> 00:35:19,999
Elyse: I'M SURE YOU GUYS
NOTICED I DID PUT ON HIGHLIGHTER

1033
00:35:19,999 --> 00:35:21,034
ON MY "CLEAVAGE."

1034
00:35:21,034 --> 00:35:23,169
Tyra: OH, YOU DID?
OH, I SEE IT.

1035
00:35:23,169 --> 00:35:24,471
IT'S SO VOLUPTUOUS. (laughs)

1036
00:35:24,471 --> 00:35:27,440
THERE IT IS.
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

1037
00:35:27,440 --> 00:35:30,410
Elyse: SEXIER THAN WHEN
I WAS IN THE BIKINI LIKE...

1038
00:35:30,410 --> 00:35:31,644
Tyra: BECAUSE IT'S YOUR TYPE
OF SEXUALITY.

1039
00:35:31,644 --> 00:35:32,879
I THINK IT'S VERY SEXY.

1040
00:35:32,879 --> 00:35:33,913
Beau: GORGEOUS,

1041
00:35:33,913 --> 00:35:35,048
GORGEOUS PICTURE.

1042
00:35:35,048 --> 00:35:36,549
♪♪♪

1043
00:35:36,549 --> 00:35:38,051
Janice: OH, MY GOD.

1044
00:35:38,051 --> 00:35:39,352
THERE SHE IS!

1045
00:35:39,352 --> 00:35:41,087
Tyra: WHOO! SHANNON!

1046
00:35:41,087 --> 00:35:44,123
Janice: LOOK WHAT
THE CAT DRAGGED IN!

1047
00:35:44,123 --> 00:35:45,859
Beau: YOU'RE FROM OHIO.

1048
00:35:45,859 --> 00:35:47,861
I'M SURE THIS IS NOT REALLY
LIKE ANYTHING YOU'VE HAD

1049
00:35:47,861 --> 00:35:49,229
TO DO ON YOURSELF BEFORE,

1050
00:35:49,229 --> 00:35:53,399
SO IT LOOKS LIKE YOU GAVE IT
A PRETTY GOOD SHOT TO ME.

1051
00:35:53,399 --> 00:35:54,868
Janice: WHOA.

1052
00:35:54,868 --> 00:35:56,436
Jay: I JUST CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU NAILED THAT LOOK.

1053
00:35:56,436 --> 00:35:57,637
EVERYTHING WAS GOING ON.

1054
00:35:57,637 --> 00:35:59,005
YOU'RE TRYING NOT TO BREAK
THE LEAF,

1055
00:35:59,005 --> 00:36:00,240
YOU HAD THAT HUGE SNAKE
COME OVER YOUR SHOULDER,

1056
00:36:00,240 --> 00:36:01,474
SO I LOVE THAT.

1057
00:36:01,474 --> 00:36:04,043
Janice: THE ATTITUDE IS GREAT.

1058
00:36:04,043 --> 00:36:05,545
I'LL GIVE YOU A 10 ON THIS ONE.

1059
00:36:05,545 --> 00:36:07,447
♪♪♪

1060
00:36:07,447 --> 00:36:09,282
- Tyra: HEY!
- Giselle: HELLO.

1061
00:36:09,282 --> 00:36:10,316
Tyra: THE MAKEUP--

1062
00:36:10,316 --> 00:36:13,219
I DON'T LIKE IT, GISELLE.
(laughs)

1063
00:36:13,219 --> 00:36:14,587
Beau: "A" FOR EFFORT.

1064
00:36:14,587 --> 00:36:17,223
I THINK THAT YOU LOOK
SO REMARKABLE IN THIS PICTURE.

1065
00:36:17,223 --> 00:36:18,858
I DIDN'T EVEN RECOGNIZE YOU
WHEN I FIRST SAW IT.

1066
00:36:18,858 --> 00:36:21,528
Giselle: I FEEL LIKE
MY FACE LOOKS TOO PLAIN.

1067
00:36:21,528 --> 00:36:23,463
Tyra: I WOULD PUT THAT UP
IN MY LIVING ROOM AS ARTWORK.

1068
00:36:23,463 --> 00:36:24,964
I THINK IT'S BEAUTIFUL.

1069
00:36:24,964 --> 00:36:26,299
Jay: YOU'RE BEAUTIFUL
ON THE OUTSIDE,

1070
00:36:26,299 --> 00:36:29,435
AND YOU JUST NEED TO HAVE
THAT THOUGHT IN YOUR MIND.

1071
00:36:29,435 --> 00:36:31,538
♪♪♪

1072
00:36:31,538 --> 00:36:33,606
- Janice: OW!
- Jay: I'M SURPRISED.

1073
00:36:33,606 --> 00:36:35,508
Kimora: YOUR EYEBROWS
LOOK GREAT.

1074
00:36:35,508 --> 00:36:37,043
YOUR EYES LOOK GREAT.

1075
00:36:37,043 --> 00:36:38,545
- IT'S PERFECT.
- Robin: THANK YOU.

1076
00:36:38,545 --> 00:36:39,612
Tyra: HERE'S
YOUR PHOTO SHOOT SHOT.

1077
00:36:39,612 --> 00:36:41,114
Robin: THAT SNAKE...

1078
00:36:41,114 --> 00:36:43,149
- Jay: (laughing)
- Robin: THERE'S THE SNAKE.

1079
00:36:43,149 --> 00:36:44,918
Kimora: I THINK
IT'S A BEAUTIFUL PICTURE.

1080
00:36:44,918 --> 00:36:45,952
YOU'RE A BEAUTIFUL GIRL.

1081
00:36:45,952 --> 00:36:47,220
Jay: I LOVE YOU, ROBIN,

1082
00:36:47,220 --> 00:36:49,923
BUT YOU JUST GIVE
SO MUCH ATTITUDE.

1083
00:36:49,923 --> 00:36:51,424
MAKEOVER DAY.

1084
00:36:51,424 --> 00:36:53,192
- OH, MY GOD, KIMORA.
- Kimora: ROBIN!

1085
00:36:53,192 --> 00:36:54,527
Tyra: SHE WAS JUST CRYIN'

1086
00:36:54,527 --> 00:36:56,563
AND ACTIN' A FOOL
AND BITCHIN' AND MOANIN'

1087
00:36:56,563 --> 00:36:58,565
AND BEIN' A DIVA,

1088
00:36:58,565 --> 00:36:59,866
BUT A DIVA IN THE WRONG,

1089
00:36:59,866 --> 00:37:01,034
NEGATIVE KIND OF WAY.

1090
00:37:01,034 --> 00:37:02,969
Robin: OKAY. I JUST--

1091
00:37:02,969 --> 00:37:03,636
Tyra: I'VE BEEN
THROUGH HAIR HELL.

1092
00:37:03,636 --> 00:37:05,305
Robin: RIGHT, EXACTLY.

1093
00:37:05,305 --> 00:37:08,508
Tyra: FRIED, DYED,
FALLIN' OUT, DREADLOCKS, AFRO,

1094
00:37:08,508 --> 00:37:11,210
PULLED BACK INTO A TIGHT BUN,

1095
00:37:11,210 --> 00:37:14,380
AND THEN FRIZZED OUT ALL IN
FIVE FASHION SHOWS IN ONE DAY.

1096
00:37:14,380 --> 00:37:15,915
JUST, THE POINT IS, ROBIN,

1097
00:37:15,915 --> 00:37:17,183
WHEN YOU GET TO THE REAL WORLD,

1098
00:37:17,183 --> 00:37:18,618
- THEY'LL JUST SAY, "BYE."
- Robin: RIGHT.

1099
00:37:20,353 --> 00:37:21,854
- Tyra: HEY, EBONY.
- Ebony: HELLO.

1100
00:37:21,854 --> 00:37:22,488
Tyra: IT LOOKS
A LITTLE CONSERVATIVE.

1101
00:37:22,488 --> 00:37:24,057
JAY, WHAT DO YOU THINK?

1102
00:37:24,057 --> 00:37:25,425
Jay: I'M ACTUALLY SURPRISED

1103
00:37:25,425 --> 00:37:27,260
AFTER YOU'VE BEEN BRAGGING
ABOUT BEING A MAKEUP ARTIST,

1104
00:37:27,260 --> 00:37:29,228
AND THEN EVERY TEST I GAVE YOU,
YOU FAILED.

1105
00:37:29,228 --> 00:37:30,163
Ebony: HONEY, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT THAT WAS.

1106
00:37:30,163 --> 00:37:32,098
Jay: I DON'T KNOW
WHAT IT WAS, EITHER.

1107
00:37:32,098 --> 00:37:34,901
Janice: I SEE NOTHING
VAGUELY SIMILAR

1108
00:37:34,901 --> 00:37:36,903
TO THIS MAKEUP WHATSOEVER.

1109
00:37:36,903 --> 00:37:38,171
Tyra: SO HERE'S YOUR SHOT.

1110
00:37:38,171 --> 00:37:39,339
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

1111
00:37:39,339 --> 00:37:40,974
Ebony: WELL, I LIKE MY SKIN.

1112
00:37:40,974 --> 00:37:42,942
Tyra: AND WITH
YOUR SKIN TEXTURE,

1113
00:37:42,942 --> 00:37:44,210
BEING AN AFRICAN-AMERICAN WOMAN,

1114
00:37:44,210 --> 00:37:45,612
IT SHOULD BE LIKE BUTTAH.

1115
00:37:45,612 --> 00:37:47,146
AT THE RETOUCHING SESSION,

1116
00:37:47,146 --> 00:37:51,417
YOUR PHOTO WAS THE HARDEST
THAT WE HAD TO DO.

1117
00:37:51,417 --> 00:37:54,220
♪♪♪

1118
00:37:54,220 --> 00:37:55,855
Tyra: GUYS, NOW IT'S TIME
TO DELIBERATE,

1119
00:37:55,855 --> 00:37:58,391
AND TO ME,
THIS WEEK IT'S VERY DIFFICULT.

1120
00:37:58,391 --> 00:37:59,926
ADRIANNE.

1121
00:37:59,926 --> 00:38:02,528
Beau: THE FACT THAT SHE
WAS SO ILL...

